{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D91-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"47c3dcbc4b244077c5666b1b482c35454de28376e14dd3d8a0f96827a0f6b945\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 explicitly compares devotion; A5 counts remembering plus archiving as superior care.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2's lack of tickets prompts A3's comparison problem; B4's memories become A5's additional category.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 defend a credible different way of remembering, but reveal little personal investment.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 adds memory to the archive claim without substantially increasing its consequence.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's twelve trip tickets establish a playable shared history and concrete evidence.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'maintained an archive' earns its dry competitiveness from A1's ticket collection.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 84\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I kept twelve tickets from our trips. How many did you keep?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"None. I made you that album instead.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"And I kept it. Your care is safe because of mine.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Open it. I put all my tickets inside.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then I'm preserving both our collections. Let me get it a waterproof cover.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A turns shared memories and their preservation into comparative evidence of caring more.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Sentimental collecting could explain keeping tickets without explaining a contest over devotion.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 asks how to 'compare devotion'; A5 claims memory and preservation together.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a competes over evidence of shared history; alternative b competes through immediate physical sacrifice.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original's 84 falls below acceptance. The revision preserves the trip setting and gives B an affectionate counterclaim. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 claims superior care), logic 5 (B2 supplies the album; B4 supplies its tickets), relationship 4 (B defends a real gift), heightening 4 (A5 assumes protection of both collections), specificity 5 (A1 and B2 establish tangible keepsakes), brevityWit 4 (A5's waterproof cover follows the preservation claim): 92. B4 makes A5's expanded custody possible.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A3's credit for keeping a gift needs sincere gratitude beneath the competitive accounting.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D91-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"ccec35bf460b06424b2dc78f8cad55d4f6b7b90e8584071372dd6e35b55efa87\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 claims greater care through carrying; A3 treats B's reciprocation as a competing claim.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2's offer becomes A3's threatened reversal; B4's sharing proposal determines A5's unequal division.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 wants to relieve A and B4 offers cooperation, forcing A to adapt.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 accepts sharing while reserving the book-heavy side as greater sacrifice.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes carrying a heavy bag; A5 supplies its unevenly weighted books.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A5's brief condition converts B4's practical solution directly into the same competition.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 92\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll carry the heavier bag. I care more about your back.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Let me take it for a while.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then you'd appear to care more about mine.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We could share it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Only if I take the side with the books.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A converts carrying and sharing a burden into proof of providing more care than B.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Generosity alone would welcome B's help without defending a superior share of sacrifice.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 explicitly fears B appearing to care more, and A5 protects the heavier share.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative uses helpful cooperation and bodily effort; alternative a uses keepsakes and competing interpretations of memory.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged after rereading the original against the card. B4's helpful sharing offer causes A5's precise condition, so cooperation develops the behavior rather than ending it. The 92 reflects that unusually economical causal finish.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The actors must make a bag with a meaningfully heavier book side easy to imagine.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D92-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"caecf46281b5f9ec7b0547e47033107b7c507b91594c66d59bf55bf9f2ee9bf9\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 treats a painful joke as shared identity; A5 treats withdrawal as continued engagement.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's painful joke, although A5 labels B4's unilateral suggestion a negotiation.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 dislikes the joke and B4 wants silence, but the relationship and occasion remain unspecified.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 transforms an attempt to stop talking into stronger evidence of connection.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1 describes awkward laughter without establishing where these people are or why they met.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'recognisably ours' is economical; A5's engagement claim follows B4's withdrawal.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 79\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Our first dinner since the breakup, and you still groan at my waiter joke.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I hoped you'd retired it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You remembered. We've still got our little traditions.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Can we eat in silence? I don't want another awful joke.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You still know how to ask me for what you need. I'll order dessert so we have time.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A interprets awkwardness and disappointment as positive evidence that the relationship is still alive.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"General optimism finds an upside; this card specifically makes the setback evidence of continuing connection.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 calls the painful joke 'ours'; A5 calls stopping conversation proof they remain engaged.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a mines discomfort during an actual reunion; alternative b mines postponements before a reunion can happen.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original lacks a sufficiently concrete occasion. The revision introduces a post-breakup dinner. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 and A5 infer intimacy), logic 5 (B2's recognition and B4's request each supply evidence), relationship 4 (B wants a tolerable dinner), heightening 4 (A5 extends the meal), specificity 5 (A1 establishes the reunion), brevityWit 4 (dessert follows the hopeful misreading): 92. B4's request for silence becomes A5's reason to prolong their time.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 should sound pleased to accommodate B, rather than pleased to defeat an objection.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D92-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"c7bb8e07a2239341bd598b413a8a1d8265ca8d5a2ae12b499d773005413504c6\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 converts postponement into hope, but A3's 'eventually' predicts connection more than proving it remains alive.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's three postponements; A5 keeps the invitation after B4 cannot name a date.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 acknowledges repeated cancellation and B4 cannot offer availability, limiting A's options.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 preserves the invitation but shifts attention from their connection to the invitation's health.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a repeatedly postponed dinner, sharpened by B2's third cancellation.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'doing remarkably well' personifies the invitation instead of sharpening the relational inference.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 75\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You've postponed dinner again. You still hate disappointing me.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's the third time. I feel awful.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"After three cancellations, my feelings still matter to you. That means something.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Please stop holding Fridays for me. I can't promise anything.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You're protecting my Fridays now. I'll leave the date open; we're already looking after each other.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A treats disappointing attempts to arrange contact as present evidence of mutual attachment.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Patient hope waits for a future relationship; this behavior claims the disappointing exchange already proves one exists.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 finds significance in having dinner to postpone, while A5 weakens that focus by praising the invitation.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative uses scheduling uncertainty and consideration at a distance; alternative a uses remembered habits during a strained dinner.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised to replace abstract future hope with evidence A extracts from B's concern. The postponed-dinner setting remains. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 and A5 claim current mutual care), logic 5 (B2's guilt and B4's release of Fridays drive each inference), relationship 4 (B wants to stop inconveniencing A), heightening 4 (A5 names reciprocal care), specificity 4 (Fridays make the cost concrete), brevityWit 4 (A5's protection claim follows the request): 90.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The ending is quietly hopeful rather than sharply comic; its success depends on A believing the inference.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D93-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"194535a5473045309647a1b3f832cb76f32da5c87d6a76d3e6724575d487fe1c\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 remembers B's tea while needling forgetfulness; A5 protects the tea while reviving the birthday grievance.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2 thanks A for remembering, prompting A3's ongoing-service claim; B4 names the birthday, enabling A5's annual jab.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 offers genuine thanks and B4 recognizes the shared grievance rather than merely feeding a joke.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 turns B4's single forgotten birthday into an 'annual discussion' while maintaining the caring pretext.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1's preferred tea and B4's forgotten birthday establish a readily playable domestic history.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 joins keeping tea warm to the duration of the grievance; A3's department metaphor is slightly conspicuous.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 86\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Here's your tea, exactly as you like it. Someone remembers preferences.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Thank you for remembering.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You're welcome. The department never closed.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Are we talking about my forgetting your birthday?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"No. Your tea would get cold during that annual discussion.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A continues familiar care while using that care to deliver an old grievance indirectly.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"A purely hostile sarcastic attack would dispense with the real attention to B's comfort.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 supplies tea exactly to B's preference; A5 keeps concern for its temperature wrapped around birthday resentment.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a lets B identify a grievance beneath hospitality; alternative b connects hands-on comfort to a specific broken promise.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged after rereading. B4 makes the grievance explicit and A5 responds by both denying the discussion and expanding its history. The concrete warmth keeps the 86 above acceptance despite the stylized A3.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A's warmth must remain audible; an exclusively icy reading would lose half the exact instruction.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D93-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"879b709a02e7b2452226b8e8c882a641e77fc9bd5fe92b74c0271df98abe3c04\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 provides a blanket and A5 agrees to loosen it, but A3's promises remain an unspecified grievance.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2's tight blanket prompts A3's tucked claim; B4's loosening request prompts A5's adjustment metaphor.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 seek physical comfort without engaging the hinted history of broken promises.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 repeats the general grievance through expectations without revealing or increasing its stakes.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes bedding, but A3's 'certain promises' gives actors no concrete shared wound.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's adjusting expectations follows B4's request neatly, though it is a familiar abstraction.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 76\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I've warmed your side of the bed, love. You sounded frozen waiting for that taxi.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You could have picked me up.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I could. Here's another blanket. I remember waiting outside your office last Christmas.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I apologised. Could you warm my feet?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Come here, love. Both feet. I wouldn't leave any part of you waiting forty minutes.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A expresses genuine domestic affection while sharpening a remembered slight through each act of care.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Punitive withholding would deny comfort; A instead supplies comfort and lets resentment travel inside it.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A5 agrees to loosen the blanket even while invoking disappointed expectations.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative b now makes the grievance bodily and reciprocal between bed-sharing partners; alternative a uses tea and a forgotten birthday.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised because the original's resentment was generic and B never addressed it. The new illustrative setting is a partner returning cold to bed. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 and A5 pair care with the old wait), logic 5 (B2 raises pickup; B4 requests foot warming), relationship 4 (B challenges A and seeks affection), heightening 4 (A5 adds forty minutes), specificity 5 (A1's taxi and A3's office establish history), brevityWit 4 (A5 transfers waiting to B's feet): 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"B2 can suggest deliberate non-collection; A's offered warmth must remain genuine rather than a disguise for punishment.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D94-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"4132bb2a79253ab6bed0b5f4d91af7a54f56375620019fa285d3c9bcc60b7030\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 prices forgiveness in opening attendance; A5 explicitly withholds release until terms are settled.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 answers B2's gift metaphor, but A5 does not price or otherwise use B4's specific work conflict.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 questions conditional forgiveness and B4 supplies a credible scheduling obstacle.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 restates the need for terms rather than changing the price when B4 cannot attend.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies an opening and required attendance, though the argument itself is unnamed.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's attendance-as-wrapping answers B2 economically; A5 is more procedural than pointed.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 79\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'll let the argument go if you come to my opening.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I thought forgiveness was a gift.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"It is. I'd like to hand it over beside my paintings.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'm working that night. I could help hang them on Sunday.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Hanging buys forgiveness. Stay to take them down and I'll stop mentioning the argument to Mum.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A assigns explicit relational benefits to favors and sacrifices as negotiable prices.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Asking for support would not make forgiveness and future discretion conditional on separate payments.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 exchanges forgiveness for attendance, while A5 withholds the argument's release pending terms.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a bargains over forgiveness and family disclosure; alternative b meters renewed access through visits and coffee.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised to make the work conflict change the actual bargain. The opening is specified as an art show, with Mum introduced as shared family pressure. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A5 prices two benefits), logic 5 (B2 shapes A3's gift; B4 supplies labor for A5), relationship 4 (B offers feasible help), heightening 4 (A5 adds a second charge), specificity 5 (paintings and installation labor are playable), brevityWit 4 (A5's itemization earns the turn): 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The added family disclosure raises the pressure; it should remain a sincere negotiation rather than a triumphant threat.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D94-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"4d0115d5f39a18714ffd2fbe07c7c572071f9946aac649562626a960bb7cbfcb\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 prices a spare key in monthly visits; A5 assigns coffee a smaller relational return.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 accepts B2's rent framing; A5 recalculates access around B4's coffee counteroffer.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 challenges the price and B4 proposes a lower-commitment way to reconnect.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 extends the ledger to charging for a discussion before the key itself.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's spare key 'again' and Sunday schedule imply a concrete history of withdrawn access.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'provisional key discussion' is a precise smaller purchase in response to B4's coffee.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You can have the spare key again for one reliable Sunday visit a month.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You're charging rent on closeness.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"A very modest calendar-based rate.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Could we start with coffee?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Certainly. Coffee earns a provisional key discussion.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A turns renewed closeness and household access into a graduated exchange for reliable attention.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Setting a reliability boundary could explain A1, but charging coffee for a preliminary discussion creates a relational price schedule.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 endorses the 'rate' and A5 assigns coffee a specific lesser entitlement.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative uses a modest counteroffer to expose finer pricing; alternative a increases the price of forgiveness through practical help.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged after rereading. B4 materially changes the proposed payment, and A5 responds with a correspondingly reduced purchase. That additional layer earns the heightening score within the original 90.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"B2 names the mechanism directly, which makes the scene clear but slightly less naturalistic.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D95-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"f18d87a2e35f33728e07549cb0ccde7b3c02165af167ba944652e0f3f2fa5d82\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 agrees to reconnect with a departure boundary; A3 substitutes that boundary for discussing the earlier departure.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's 'why you left'; A5 answers B4's distinction only through a general statement.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 wants to address the rupture and B4 refuses to equate it with tonight's logistics.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 explains the existing limit without adding a tactic, condition or consequence after B4's correction.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes dinner and ten o'clock; B2 supplies the unresolved departure.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 has a clear verbal pivot, but A5 becomes an explanatory statement of the premise.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 78\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Yes, let's reconnect. I'll come for dinner and leave at ten.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We need to discuss why you left.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Of course. Put that before pudding so we finish on something nice.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"What if I'm still upset at ten?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then we'll book another dinner. I want us to keep seeing each other without either evening running over.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A agrees to relationship repair while reshaping its timing and emotional demands around personally convenient limits.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Simply refusing reconciliation would not include A's repeated offers of continued contact.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 says 'let's reconnect'; A3 moves the requested discussion onto A's preferred departure terms.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a controls the timetable of repeated repair meetings; alternative b reduces the format and redirects unresolved material.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised because original A5 merely explains the boundary. Dinner remains the setting. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 schedules hurt and A5 limits it), logic 5 (B2 determines the agenda; B4 causes another dinner), relationship 4 (B wants adequate emotional time), heightening 4 (A5 makes the cap govern future meetings), specificity 4 (pudding and ten anchor the terms), brevityWit 4 (A5's caring invitation carries the restriction): 90.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A's convenient scheduling could read as reasonable boundaries unless the desire to compress B's distress remains evident.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D95-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"554deb35233d93fb5fa065c8c4f064ba99f5907283cd7abf7320b7464998639d\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 agrees to time together while excluding old arguments; A3 reduces the weekend when B insists on repair.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2's reason for the weekend causes A3's afternoon; A5 acknowledges B4 without making a further adjustment.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 insists the arguments are the purpose and B4 identifies A's retreat.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 justifies the shrinking already achieved in A3 rather than developing it.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies a weekend and separate rooms; A3 offers a clear shorter alternative.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'pleasant afternoon' is an earned reduction; A5 is concise but largely explanatory.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 83\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'd love a weekend to patch things up. Separate rooms, though, and no old arguments.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The old arguments are why we need the weekend.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then let's start with a pleasant afternoon. We can rebuild from there.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I can't fit everything I need to say into an afternoon.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Send the rest by email. I'll read it when I'm ready, and we can keep the afternoon for us.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A accepts repairing the relationship while redefining closeness to preserve control over difficult engagement.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Simple avoidance would end contact; A actively protects pleasant contact by relocating its burdens elsewhere.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 wants another weekend, but A3 replaces it with an afternoon when B names its difficult purpose.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative changes duration and communication medium; alternative a preserves dinner while controlling emotional time within it.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised to turn B4 into a concrete constraint and A5 into a fresh accommodating restriction. The weekend proposal remains. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A5 retains contact while controlling receipt of grievances), logic 5 (B2 prompts shortening; B4 prompts email), relationship 4 (B needs sufficient space), heightening 4 (A5 also controls when to read), specificity 4 (rooms, afternoon and email are playable), brevityWit 4 (A5's 'for us' recasts exclusion as intimacy): 90.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The email proposal should be offered with real hope of repair, not as an obvious dismissal.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D96-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"022ed9e5db47928bcf987ef2e9a116cb0fb9f06cb2eeb6eb9c64ef59d2fa5188\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 identifies repeated waiting, but A5 requests a change without raising a concrete consequence.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 distinguishes B2's new battery explanation from the old result; A5 directly challenges B4's repeated promise.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 offers a situational defense and B4 tries reassurance, giving A two different responses to challenge.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'choose what changes' adds a demand but leaves the cost of another failure unspecified.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's promised call and B2's dead battery establish an immediate recognizable dispute.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's changed explanation and unchanged waiting are economical; A5's reused sentence follows B4.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 73\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You promised to call. I kept dinner warm until eleven again.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"This time my battery died.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Last time it was the train. Different explanation, same ruined dinner. Tomorrow I'm eating at seven.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll borrow a phone next time. Please keep a plate for me.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"That's how I end up waiting again. Miss another call and you're buying and cooking your own dinners.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A treats each new defense as another instance of a recurring relationship pattern and escalates its cost.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ordinary boundary setting can respond to one incident; this card repeatedly uses the incident as proof of an established cycle.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 separates a changed explanation from unchanged waiting, but A5 lacks the required raised consequence.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a escalates the practical cost of waiting at home; alternative b escalates responsibility and social risk around cancelled visits.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised to supply the missing consequence, introducing dinner waiting as the concrete cost of the missed call. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 and A5 identify recurrence and raise costs), logic 5 (B2 supplies the excuse; B4 asks to preserve the waiting arrangement), relationship 4 (B offers a remedy and wants dinner), heightening 4 (A5 withdraws future cooking), specificity 5 (eleven, seven and the saved plate ground the dispute), brevityWit 3 (A5 is forceful rather than especially witty): 90.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A's suspicion rejects a plausible practical remedy; the scene needs conviction in the history rather than proof B is objectively wrong.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D96-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"74c34168a38ee5f1f5a4d4df5b48e19d5779cfb6356faa5ec8efc4121f7b15b9\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 invokes a repeated cancellation and A3 transfers scheduling responsibility, but A5 only announces change.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 responds to B2 by assigning the next date; A5 uses B4's trust language without specifying a new action.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 defends the cancellation and B4 challenges its implications for trust.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'changing my part' adds no consequence beyond A3's existing scheduling condition.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 mentions a rearranged week but provides no visit purpose or concrete rearrangement.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5's trust-the-pattern formulation is compact but sounds like an abstract concluding maxim.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 70\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You're cancelling Sunday again? Mum's already made up the spare bed.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Work changed my shift. I can't help it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Last time it was overtime. Same empty bed, same explanation from me. You tell her this time.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"She'll think I don't want to visit. Could you soften it?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"That's the pattern: you cancel, I soften. Now you can arrange the next visit with her too.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A uses the latest disagreement to establish a repeating relational division of labor and increases B's responsibility.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Delegating one awkward call would pursue immediate relief; A instead treats the request as proof of a cycle and expands the consequences.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A1 cites 'another' cancellation and A5 explicitly trusts the pattern, but does not specify the increased cost.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative places siblings between cancellation and their mother's disappointment; alternative a concerns a partner's recurring dinner wait.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised to make the repeating role and raised consequence playable. The new illustrative setting is a cancelled family visit. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 and A5 name the cycle and transfer more responsibility), logic 5 (B2 supplies work; B4 requests the old mediation), relationship 4 (B fears hurting Mum), heightening 4 (A5 adds future arrangements), specificity 5 (Sunday and the spare bed ground the cost), brevityWit 4 (A5's paired verbs summarize demonstrated behavior): 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The family setting introduces a third person's expectations, but all action remains in the spoken exchange between A and B.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D97-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"ea2e07206cffcf73febf4d4f95e6cbdf72e14a407274fbffb69215e16166bdcf\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 asks B to remove one burden instead of answering what's wrong; A5 permits support without naming its weight.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 redirects B2's inquiry toward the call; A5 conditionally accepts B4's offer to talk afterward.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 seeks understanding, then B4 offers a gentler sequence rather than demanding disclosure.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 opens the possibility of further emotional support after the initial practical delegation.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 gives B a concrete cancellation call, though the booking's emotional significance remains withheld.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'one thing lighter' develops A3's 'take off me' without explaining the underlying crisis.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Could you make this one call for me? Just say the booking's cancelled.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"What's wrong?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Please let the call be the first thing you take off me.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Do you want to talk afterward?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Maybe. One thing lighter might make room.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A recruits practical help as a share of emotional weight while avoiding a declaration of how overwhelmed they are.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Start the Hard Part delegates a difficult beginning; this exchange also negotiates ongoing support without requiring disclosure.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 asks for the call before answering B2's inquiry, and A5 leaves further talking conditional on the relief it creates.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a delegates an outward-facing cancellation and cautiously opens conversation; alternative b asks B to absorb a letter's first impact and remain present.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged after rereading. B4's offer changes the possible support from a single task to subsequent conversation, and A5 accepts that possibility without naming the burden. Its quiet development supports the original 90.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The unspecified booking requires actors to supply emotional stakes privately; the spoken task itself