ial reactions or protection from questions about delay.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 makes B's emotional reaction a condition of hearing the letter; the revised A5 requests shared handling without explanation.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative shares the immediate experience of reading; alternative a outsources a cancellation before considering later conversation.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised to replace the lighting joke with practical shared emotional labor, preserving the exact first three turns and letter setting. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 manages impact; A5 avoids disclosure), logic 5 (B2 causes the condition; B4's pace causes guided reading), relationship 4 (B offers attuned support), heightening 4 (A5 adds holding and guiding), specificity 4 (the page and finger are playable), brevityWit 4 (A5's practical requests expose the need indirectly): 90.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The letter remains deliberately unspecified, and the revised ending earns tenderness more than a strong laugh.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D98-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"320cc7262d2d0895e45de39aa0066d6040779efefb85b409e7312ca791edd4e9\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 links staying to unsteady hands after news; A5 asks for one manageable minute before B leaves.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's three cups to normalize a fourth; A5 reduces the request when B4 announces the taxi.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 registers the extended stay and B4 supplies a real departure constraint.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5 drops the tea pretext and makes B's imminent departure the explicit pressure on becoming steady.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's hands and tea provide physical anchors; B4's taxi makes departure immediate.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's fourth-cup logic grows from B2; A5's 'still only outside' precisely locates the remaining reprieve.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Stay for one more tea. My hands haven't caught up with the news.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"We've had three cups.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then the fourth needs no explanation.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"My taxi's outside.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Let me manage one quiet minute while it's still only outside.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A extends B's physical presence in progressively more direct bids for enough steadiness to endure the departure.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Wanting company indefinitely lacks the card's readiness threshold; A asks for a manageable interval tied to immediate distress.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 names unsteady hands after news, and A5 asks to manage one quiet minute as B4's taxi threatens departure.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a bargains against external time pressure; alternative b turns B's helpful patience into staged practice for being alone.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged after rereading. B4 collapses the available time, causing A5 to abandon another cup and ask directly for a minute of steadiness. Increased exposure rather than a larger time request earns the heightening score.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"What comes after the news stays implicit, and 'hands haven't caught up' is somewhat literary.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D98-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"1c45f990c38c8cd9b2ee2f1dea33c956fad76d4920ebc77b6bdebc73085c8429\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 keeps B at the door and A3 tests breathing without checking, though the next challenge is unspecified.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2 completes the first five, prompting A3's harder five; A5 directly acknowledges B4's standing there.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 cooperates with counting and B4 offers continued presence, enabling rather than opposing A.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 explains why B's presence helps but makes no next attempt toward readiness.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a door and breaths, but gives no situation beyond an impending exit.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's five without checking is a precise development; A5 is concise but mostly explanatory.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 76\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Before you leave me in the new flat, count five breaths with me.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"That was five. Shall I close the door?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Not yet. Five more while I look at the empty kitchen instead of you.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll wait here while you put the kettle on.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Stay until it boils. Then I'll try pouring one cup without getting yours out.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A keeps B nearby while testing increasingly concrete steps toward managing the next moments alone.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"General dependence seeks continuing availability; A ties requests to specific rehearsals of independence.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 requests breaths without checking for B, showing a readiness test that original A5 does not develop.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative uses cooperative practice in a new home; alternative a negotiates a shrinking interval before a waiting taxi leaves.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised to develop readiness after B's helpful offer. A new flat supplies the illustrative setting. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 and A5 test coping alone), logic 5 (B2 causes a harder breath sequence; B4's kettle causes the pouring test), relationship 4 (B offers practical patience), heightening 4 (A5 faces the one-cup reality), specificity 5 (empty kitchen and kettle ground the transition), brevityWit 4 (one cup carries the emotional consequence): 92.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The reason A now lives alone remains open, allowing different relationships without requiring a spoken backstory.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D99-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"3459170f1f871574fb7c8f3406709e5811ad9fc7d50643e882fbb03944972e76\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 explains the repeated looking at the door; A5 prioritizes feeling unimportant over logistics.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 directly uses B2's busyness, but A5 introduces a train timetable neither B2 nor B4 mentioned.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 initially defends the absence, then B4 attempts a real acknowledgment of its meaning.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 accepts B4's diagnosis but pivots to unsupported travel logistics instead of deepening it.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1's saved seat and A3's watching the door make the hurt playable despite the unnamed event.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's waiting image is economical; A5's timetable line reaches for a contrast outside the established exchange.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 77\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I saved you a front-row seat at my concert. Do you understand why it hurt?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I told you work might run late.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I knew. I still looked at that empty seat before every song.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You needed someone there who knew what this meant to you.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Yes. You'd heard me practise for months. Please tell me you understand why someone else couldn't fill it.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"A presses B to acknowledge the personal meaning of their absence rather than merely its factual explanation.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Seeking an apology alone could end with regret; A asks B to understand why this particular person's absence mattered.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 distinguishes knowing B was busy from repeatedly looking for B, and B4 names the resulting feeling.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a concerns irreplaceable presence at a milestone; alternative b concerns silence being interpreted as loss of care.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised to remove the unseeded timetable and deepen B4's acknowledgment. The saved-seat event is specified as A's concert. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A5 asks for the specific meaning), logic 5 (B2's warning shapes A3; B4's understanding prompts the practice history), relationship 4 (B moves from defense to empathy), heightening 4 (A5 specifies irreplaceability), specificity 5 (front row, songs and practice ground the hurt), brevityWit 3 (emotionally clear but little verbal surprise): 90.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 asks for further acknowledgment after B has already understood much of the hurt; it should deepen connection rather than move the goalposts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D99-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"0f165f7aafe01f02b8d639ab1184c3e1f7f8ba0848